Check C stack usage in ReadItem_Recursive(), so a deeply nested
serialized stream raises an R error instead of overflowing the stack.

ReadItem_Recursive() (src/main/serialize.c) recurses once per level of
nesting in the stream; a stream nesting pairlist or list items tens of
thousands deep (50 KB is enough) segfaults.  R_CheckStack() on entry
raises the usual "C stack usage is too close to the limit" error.

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R),
not carried here.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 6214305381679104 (afl_asan_r,
Stack-overflow in ReadItem_Recursive).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #373, filed 2026-10-10 (no Bugzilla
report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/serialize.c
+++ b/src/main/serialize.c
@@ -1894,6 +1894,11 @@
 
     R_assert(TYPEOF(ref_table) == LISTSXP && TYPEOF(CAR(ref_table)) == VECSXP);
 
+    /* Each level of nesting in the stream recurses here, so a stream
+       nesting lists tens of thousands deep would otherwise overflow the
+       C stack before anything else notices. */
+    R_CheckStack();
+
     UnpackFlags(flags, &type, &levs, &objf, &hasattr, &hastag);
 
     switch(type) {
